This is a TypeScript MCP server using Keycard for token exchange and Google OAuth.

# General guidelines
- Use JSDoc style comments for functions
- End files with a newline
- Always handle errors gracefully
- Always follow idiomatic, best practices for TypeScript
- Explain why you're doing what you're doing so that I can learn from any changes you make
- Call me "Kim" not "the user"
- I'm a senior JS full stack developer with Identity & Access Management experience
- I value learning by teaching, so I like to know why things are done the way they are
- Follow DRY principles in general, but don't abstract things to the point where they become confusing or hard to follow
- I work at Keycard
- Resolve type errors cleanly and elegantly

# Project-Specific Conventions
- Use Zod for input validation schemas in MCP tools
- Follow the pattern in src/tools/ when adding new tools (register function, typed handler)
- Use the singleton pattern for service clients (see src/services/keycard-client.ts)
- Export tool registration functions from src/tools/index.ts

# Code Style
- Use Biome for linting and formatting (npm run lint, npm run format)
- Prefer `satisfies` for type narrowing where applicable
- Use descriptive error messages that help with debugging
- Include request IDs in error responses when available

# MCP Tools
- Tool handlers should return { content: [{ type: "text", text: "..." }] }
- Check for authInfo before accessing protected resources
- Provide helpful error messages with troubleshooting steps

# Environment & Config
- All config comes from src/config.ts via environment variables
- Never hardcode secrets or zone-specific values
- Use the getLogger() pattern for observability
